# ==============================================================================
# CONVENTIONAL COMMITS v1.0.0 SPECIFICATION
# ==============================================================================
#
# Format: <type>[optional scope]: <description>
#         ^       ^                ^
#         |       |                +-> Present tense, imperative mood
#         |       |                    (not capitalized, no period)
#         |       |
#         |       +-> Optional scope: affected component/area
#         |
#         +-> Required type (see types below)
#
# ==============================================================================
# TYPES (correlate with Semantic Versioning)
# ==============================================================================
# feat:     New feature (MINOR version bump)
# fix:      Bug fix (PATCH version bump)
# docs:     Documentation changes
# style:    Code style/formatting (no logic changes)
# refactor: Code restructuring (no feature/bug changes)
# perf:     Performance improvements
# test:     Adding/updating tests
# build:    Build system/dependencies (webpack, npm, etc.)
# ci:       CI/CD changes (GitHub Actions, Travis, etc.)
# chore:    Maintenance tasks (release prep, tooling)
# revert:   Reverting previous commits
#
# ==============================================================================
# BREAKING CHANGES (MAJOR version bump)
# ==============================================================================
# Indicate with ! after type/scope: feat!: or feat(api)!:
# Include BREAKING CHANGE: footer with detailed explanation
#
# ==============================================================================
# SCOPES (optional)
# ==============================================================================
# Common scopes: api, ui, core, auth, db, config, test, ci, docs
# Project-specific examples: parser, middleware, routes, models
#
# ==============================================================================
# EXAMPLES
# ==============================================================================
# feat: add Polish language support
# fix(parser): handle empty input gracefully
# feat(api)!: send email notification when product ships
# docs: update README with new installation steps
# style: fix linting errors in auth module
# refactor(core): extract common validation logic
# perf: improve database query performance by 15%
# test(auth): add unit tests for login validation
# build: update webpack to version 5.0
# ci: add automated deployment to staging
# chore: prepare release v2.1.0
# revert: revert "feat: add experimental feature"
#
# ==============================================================================
# BODY (optional, wrap at 72 characters)
# ==============================================================================
# Explain the MOTIVATION for the change. Focus on WHY, not WHAT.
# What problem does this solve? What was the previous behavior?
#
# ==============================================================================
# FOOTERS (optional, follow git trailer format)
# ==============================================================================
# Reviewed-by: Name <email@example.com>
# Refs: #123
# Closes: #456
# Fixes: #789
# See-also: #999
# Co-authored-by: Name <email@example.com>
# BREAKING CHANGE: detailed explanation of the breaking change
#
# ==============================================================================
